# TypeScript / React

- Match existing style: functional components, named exports for screens/components, TypeScript types colocated or in shared `types/` when introduced.
- Prefer existing contexts over prop-drilling session/permissions.
- Do not add `useMemo` / `useCallback` by default; use when matching nearby code or fixing a real dependency issue.
- Keep route definitions in `routes.tsx`; guards via `ProtectedRoute` / `Guarded`.
- Avoid new default dependencies unless needed (no axios if `fetch` client is established; no UI kit takeover).
- Remove or avoid dead imports when touching files; do not mass-delete orphan screens without asking.
- When introducing files under `api/` or `server/`, keep UI files free of DB imports.
